      "source": [
        "Think of it like this\n",
        "\n",
        "For January:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$ 2x_{\\text{Laptop,Jan}} +3x_{\\text{Smartphone,Jan}} +1x_{\\text{Tablet,Jan}} +\\cdots +4x_{\\text{Scanner,Jan}} \\leq 300 $$\n",
        "\n",
        "One equation → one constraint.\n",
        "\n",
        "Then we create another one for February and another for March.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Objective Function\n",
        "\n",
        "We want to **minimize the total cost**, which consists of three components:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Production Cost**  \n",
        "   Cost of producing each product in each month.\n",
        "\n",
        "2. **Inventory Holding Cost**  \n",
        "   Cost of keeping products in inventory from one month to the next.\n",
        "\n",
        "3. **Backlog Cost**  \n",
        "   Cost/penalty for satisfying demand in a later month.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Mathematical Formulation\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\min Z =\n",
        "\\sum_{p \\in P}\\sum_{m \\in M}\n",
        "\\left(\n",
        "C^P_p x_{p,m}\n",
        "+\n",
        "C^I_p I_{p,m}\n",
        "+\n",
        "C^B_p B_{p,m}\n",
        "\\right)\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "where:\n",
        "\n",
        "- $x_{p,m}$ = production quantity of product $p$ in month $m$\n",
        "- $I_{p,m}$ = inventory quantity of product $p$ at the end of month $m$\n",
        "- $B_{p,m}$ = backlog quantity of product $p$ at the end of month $m$\n",
        "- $C^P_p$ = production cost per unit of product $p$\n",
        "- $C^I_p$ = inventory holding cost per unit of product $p$\n",
        "- $C^B_p$ = backlog cost per unit of product $p$\n",
        "- $P$ = set of products\n",
        "- $M$ = set of months\n",
        "\n",
        "Therefore:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\boxed{\n",
        "\\text{Total Cost}\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\text{Production Cost}\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\text{Inventory Holding Cost}\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\text{Backlog Cost}\n",
        "}\n",
        "$$"
      ],
